{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1434223-are-mummies-still-canon","id":1434223,"title":"Are Mummies still Canon?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-02-01T21:23:16-08:00","id":1434223,"title":"Are Mummies still Canon?","content":"Are they? I am curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T21:55:16-08:00","id":1434225,"title":"","content":"I know they've been referenced in WoD20a material, at least.<br /> <br /> Issue being that with the state of things, I don't think we're getting a Mummy 20th Anniversary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T22:38:05-08:00","id":1434226,"title":"","content":"Good to know. I ask because I have a VtM plot line invovling a hedge mage mummifying some kindred and it got me thinking about actual mummies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T22:42:09-08:00","id":1434227,"title":"","content":"Define Mummy and canon because both are all over the place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T22:59:06-08:00","id":1434228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1434223-are-mummies-still-canon?p=1434227#post1434227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Define Mummy and canon because both are all over the place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mummy: the undying who have been subject some iteration of the Spell of Life.<br /> <br /> Canon is trickier now that I think about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T05:18:49-08:00","id":1434252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1434223-are-mummies-still-canon?p=1434228#post1434228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mummy: the undying who have been subject some iteration of the Spell of Life.<br /> <br /> Canon is trickier now that I think about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>the pre-Reckoning immortals from 1st and 2nd ed or the post-Reckoning ones from Resurrection?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T09:36:43-08:00","id":1434264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1434223-are-mummies-still-canon?p=1434252#post1434252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> the pre-Reckoning immortals from 1st and 2nd ed or the post-Reckoning ones from Resurrection?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This.. and then once you get into that you have the other cultures of M:TR that don't fit but are called Mummies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T10:03:59-08:00","id":1434267,"title":"","content":"Reckoning is the Maelstrom?<br /> <br /> This musing definitely includes the South American and Wu T'ian variants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T18:37:49-08:00","id":1434324,"title":"","content":"They're as canonical as you want them to be. I don't think we have any sort of official fan organization or anything that decides such things. So you can use the original ones (including or excluding the Chinese and American immortals), the Resurrection ones, or ignore them altogether as you see fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T18:54:34-08:00","id":1434331,"title":"","content":"Fair. I just try to be mindful of these sorts of things.<br /> <br /> My first RPG experiences were on Krynn so being mindful of the canon without letting it get in the way is something I've geared to since an early age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T02:53:42-08:00","id":1434363,"title":"","content":"They appear to be. Anecdotally i have a Mummy pc in my WoD crossover game. She's doing pretty well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3399-hachiman","name":"hachiman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3399_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T09:37:59-08:00","id":1434390,"title":"","content":"Since Onyx Path does not have the license to create a Mummy 20th Anniversary Edition they have been limited to small references. I backed the WoD Ghost Hunters Kickstarter just because it has a write-up of the Ashukhi Corporation from Mummy: the Resurrection.<br /> <br /> Early on, new White Wolf mentioned planning to add Mummy to their One World Of Darkness, but who knows if that is still the case. If it is, it is a long way off.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T09:40:50-08:00","id":1434391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hachiman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1434223-are-mummies-still-canon?p=1434363#post1434363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They appear to be. Anecdotally i have a Mummy pc in my WoD crossover game. She's doing pretty well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a couple of mummy NPCs in my ongoing Werewolf game. One they know about (although, in character, they are a bit clueless since the NPC Silent Strider left out some details on purpose) but the other is a plot whammy I am keeping quiet for now. Crossover can be so much fun if you play your cards correctly.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T10:33:28-08:00","id":1434399,"title":"","content":"Mummies have to be canon to some degree given the backstory with the Followers of Set and the Children of Osiris. They\u2019re certainly more balanced for a Vampire campaign than introducing a Mage or Garou would be.<br /> <br /> For quick-and-dirty version in V20 give them a \u201cGeneration\u201d but run it in reverse (a newly risen mummy is \u201c8th Gen\u201d while one nearly ready to go back to the Underworld to recharge is \u201c13th Gen\u201d), replace Blood with Sekhem (recharges X per day at sunrise) and limit them to the Auspex, Necromancy and Thaumaturgy disciples. They can heal by spending Sekhem like Vamps spend blood and take no damage from sunlight, but fire is still aggravated and they can\u2019t feed to quickly recover Blood/Sekhem either. Torpor is normal (except their spirit is in the underworld) and Final Death drops them into Torpor/the Underworld as if their Humanity were 4 points lower (so a saintly Humanity 10 can return in a month, a Humanity 7 in half-a-century, and 4 or less needs a millennium).<br /> <br /> That\u2019s nowhere near as exact as having the actual rules, but it\u2019s \u201cclose enough\u201d for most campaigns; particularly if you want to keep your players on relatively even ground and don\u2019t want to deal with a lot of different mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T13:59:51-08:00","id":1434418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1434223-are-mummies-still-canon?p=1434399#post1434399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mummies have to be canon to some degree given the backstory with the Followers of Set and the Children of Osiris. They\u2019re certainly more balanced for a Vampire campaign than introducing a Mage or Garou would be.<br /> <br /> For quick-and-dirty version in V20 give them a \u201cGeneration\u201d but run it in reverse (a newly risen mummy is \u201c8th Gen\u201d while one nearly ready to go back to the Underworld to recharge is \u201c13th Gen\u201d), replace Blood with Sekhem (recharges X per day at sunrise) and limit them to the Auspex, Necromancy and Thaumaturgy disciples. They can heal by spending Sekhem like Vamps spend blood and take no damage from sunlight, but fire is still aggravated and they can\u2019t feed to quickly recover Blood/Sekhem either. Torpor is normal (except their spirit is in the underworld) and Final Death drops them into Torpor/the Underworld as if their Humanity were 4 points lower (so a saintly Humanity 10 can return in a month, a Humanity 7 in half-a-century, and 4 or less needs a millennium).<br /> <br /> That\u2019s nowhere near as exact as having the actual rules, but it\u2019s \u201cclose enough\u201d for most campaigns; particularly if you want to keep your players on relatively even ground and don\u2019t want to deal with a lot of different mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>So mummies in WoD have the same, getting weaker with time aspect that mummies in CoD do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T15:28:54-08:00","id":1434425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1434223-are-mummies-still-canon?p=1434418#post1434418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So mummies in WoD have the same, getting weaker with time aspect that mummies in CoD do?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how its down in CoD, but in WoD, Mummies spend time in the underworld gathering spiritual energy that they use to bring their mortal body to life. Over time that energy depletes and their spirit has to go back into the underworld to recharge again... during which time the body is usually secured in some type of tomb for safekeeping.<br /> <br /> By default a mummy loses 1 point of this energy every decade with a maximum of 10 stored if memory serves... but that's assuming they lead a quiet uneventful life; if they need to use magic or rapidly heal they can burn through it pretty quickly... thus PCs often bounce between the living world and the underworld pretty regularly because its possible to gather the energy needed in short order if you're motivated, but the default NPC mummy spends years or even decades gathering the energy needed as a sort of extended holiday.<br /> <br /> Note too that WoD mummies are utterly immortal. Even if only a hint of ash remains of their old body, the mummy can spend the spiritual energy they gather to reconstitute it (possibly taking several gathering attempts to get enough to fully restore it). Do enough damage though and most NPC mummies will be out of your hair for a couple decades or even centuries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T05:29:02-08:00","id":1434478,"title":"","content":"This thread makes me want a Mummy &quot;5th&quot; Edition, that makes mummies not more common but more general as to what they can be or where they come from. And even though not much is being stated about the Maelstrom and all that in V5, it's safe to assume that the Underworld is still a stormy mess, and many things can either wake up or be put to sleep.<br /> I believe mummies could be more akin to Mummy the Curse and Vampires (or even Wan Kuei that only wake up after thousands of years). And be possible in every continent.<br /> <br /> But, it doesn't seem Mummies were uncanonized. Not really. But things like the Wan Kuei, I would say yes, you don't hear nothing from them in a long long time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T14:15:21-08:00","id":1434528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1434223-are-mummies-still-canon?p=1434425#post1434425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how its down in CoD, but in WoD, Mummies spend time in the underworld gathering spiritual energy that they use to bring their mortal body to life. Over time that energy depletes and their spirit has to go back into the underworld to recharge again...</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1434223-are-mummies-still-canon?p=1434425#post1434425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By default a mummy loses 1 point of this energy every decade with a maximum of 10 stored if memory serves...</div> </div> </div> </div>This was true in the earlier editions does not seem to be the case as of Mummy: the Resurrection. Amenti live an ageless life of 60 years plus ~10 per level of teh BA background unless killed (see the BA background description on page 64 of Mummy the Resurrection. Of course, use whichever option works best for you.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T14:17:03-08:00","id":1434529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1434223-are-mummies-still-canon?p=1434418#post1434418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So mummies in WoD have the same, getting weaker with time aspect that mummies in CoD do?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, WoD Mummies maintain full potency throughout their life cycle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-05T07:34:54-08:00","id":1434598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThomasM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1434223-are-mummies-still-canon?p=1434529#post1434529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, WoD Mummies maintain full potency throughout their life cycle.</div> </div> </div> </div>As pointed out in the previous post; yes and no.<br /> <br /> Mummy: The Resurrection completely changed Mummies from the ground up. The entire premise there was that 1-2e mummies\u2019 souls were ground up and spackled onto the souls of recently deceased modern people... basically making them yet another \u201cyou used to be a normal person, but now you\u2019ve become [insert splat title here] in a hopeless struggle against the End Times\u201d that was pretty much the sum total of the Revised-era oWoD creative process.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think I even finished the Resurrection core book... it was another creatively exhausted paint-by-numbers (right down to 5-9 archetypes with boon, flaw and magic focus) splat that had only superficial associations with the pre-Revised concept.<br /> <br /> I much prefer original recipe Mummy; you are actually an ancient being who has lived through history and must struggle with maintaining their memories and finding purpose in an endless life (and could therefore be inserted into any oWoD game as their themes work on a personal level regardless of the splat-related themes they\u2019re joining into). It was something unique as a player option in the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> As such, my knowledge of and experience with Mummies is almost entirely the 1-2e varieties (where Ba did degrade with time).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T20:28:09-07:00","id":1441189,"title":"","content":"Great to see a few people who understand about Mummy The Resurrection!!<br /> I'm currently playing a campaign with other 4 friends (+ GM) and we really liked the &quot;good guys felling&quot;. <br /> <br /> Do you guys know if there's an errata for the book? <br /> I just found this link with some Question and Answer: <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20070224035441/http://www.white-wolf.com/Games/Pages/MummyPreview/MummyFAQ.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://web.archive.org/web/20070224.../MummyFAQ.html</a><br /> But I really doubt that's all there is to fix the game.<br /> <br /> Or some advice about broken stuff that we would be advised to stay away from?<br /> Or even Tips on how to play it better? Like &quot;don't forget to use Relic, they are very good&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you like Alchemicals, please check out my DeviantArt Gallery!! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> - 5 Magic Materials BeamKlaves and Gyroscopic Chakrans ? OK<br /> - Autochthonia updated World Map? OK<br /> And many more! <a href=\"http://efq.deviantart.com/gallery/48131405/Alchemicals\" target=\"_blank\">http://efq.deviantart.com/gallery/48131405/Alchemicals</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2498-yukiartic","name":"Yukiartic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-06T08:24:18-07:00","id":1442839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yukiartic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1434223-are-mummies-still-canon?p=1441189#post1441189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great to see a few people who understand about Mummy The Resurrection!!<br /> I'm currently playing a campaign with other 4 friends (+ GM) and we really liked the &quot;good guys felling&quot;.<br /> <br /> Do you guys know if there's an errata for the book?<br /> I just found this link with some Question and Answer: <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20070224035441/http://www.white-wolf.com/Games/Pages/MummyPreview/MummyFAQ.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://web.archive.org/web/20070224.../MummyFAQ.html</a><br /> But I really doubt that's all there is to fix the game.<br /> <br /> Or some advice about broken stuff that we would be advised to stay away from?<br /> Or even Tips on how to play it better? Like &quot;don't forget to use Relic, they are very good&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly there isn't any additional errata of which I am aware. As I remember, the Mummy Players' Guide retconned a couple of things, but did not include true errata.<br /> <br /> My best tips as a ST are:<br /> <br /> * Give your players lots of Background points. The Backgrounds, like in Mage, are VITAL. You can award them during play as the characters develop or you can let them have them all up front. I leaned toward the former when I ran my game.<br /> <br /> * If the game is not set in the lands of faith, consider easing the difficulty of regaining Sekhem. Otherwise it is prohibitively difficult.<br /> <br /> * Consider adding in custom &quot;additions&quot; to the Web of Faith. Perhaps the Shemsu Heru or other ancient mummies built temples around the world that could be used as both pilgrimage sites and refueling stations for the Arisen.<br /> <br /> * If there will be vampires in your chronicle make sure someone has sufficient ranks in the Celestial Hekau and purchases the Sahu Ra spell. It is your friend. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Do you or your group have any specific questions we can answer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T04:59:56-07:00","id":1443864,"title":"","content":"Pillars of Ma'at updates MtR to 20th anniversary and touches on updating older versions as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/267119/Pillars-of-Maat\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/1/267119.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/267119/Pillars-of-Maat\" target=\"_blank\"> Pillars of Ma'at - White Wolf | DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/267119/Pillars-of-Maat\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/267119/Pillars-of-Maat </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Pillars of Ma'at - The Amenti are Reborn! The Amenti are the latest incarnations of the undying servants of Osiris, detailed in&nbsp;Mummy: Th </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T11:44:10-07:00","id":1443905,"title":"","content":"Damian,<br /> Thank you very much. I had no idea this product existed on the Storyteller's Vault and am buying it now! Now I know that you have to go to the Storyteller's Vault before searching for Mummy products for it to come up. Live and learn...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T02:17:06-07:00","id":1444466,"title":"","content":"Aren't mummies mentioned in the TBH 20th book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T13:30:57-07:00","id":1444538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1434223-are-mummies-still-canon?p=1444466#post1444466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't mummies mentioned in the TBH 20th book?</div> </div> </div> </div>TBH V20 leaned pretty hard on Inauhaten's true nature being something of a mystery to the TMR. Something powerful, knowledgeable about and connected to the Underworld, but whether or not he was a Shemsu-Heru is considered up for debate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T07:32:02-07:00","id":1445662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1434223-are-mummies-still-canon?p=1444466#post1444466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't mummies mentioned in the TBH 20th book?</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct. There are quick and dirty stats for Mummies akin to the antagonist supernaturals in the back of the core book that take about 3/4 of a pagenear the tail end of the Black Hand V20 book. The quick and dirty stats use thaumaturgy paths in place of mummy-specific abilities (only burning \u201cSekham\u201d instead of blood )which is honestly \u201cgood enough\u201d for play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T11:48:38-07:00","id":1445688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1434223-are-mummies-still-canon?p=1445662#post1445662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are correct. There are quick and dirty stats for Mummies akin to the antagonist supernaturals in the back of the core book that take about 3/4 of a pagenear the tail end of the Black Hand V20 book. The quick and dirty stats use thaumaturgy paths in place of mummy-specific abilities (only burning \u201cSekham\u201d instead of blood )which is honestly \u201cgood enough\u201d for play.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is actually a really handy find, thank you for pointing that out!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T18:33:26-07:00","id":1446384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1434223-are-mummies-still-canon?p=1434267#post1434267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reckoning is the Maelstrom?<br /> <br /> This musing definitely includes the South American and Wu T'ian variants.</div> </div> </div> </div>They mean are you asking about the immortal ancient Egyptians from Mummy 1st edition and Mummy 2nd edition; or are you asking about the Amenti from Mummy the Resurrection who are modern day people who have had a piece of an ancient Egyptian soul shoved into them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T18:36:58-07:00","id":1446385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1434223-are-mummies-still-canon?p=1434418#post1434418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So mummies in WoD have the same, getting weaker with time aspect that mummies in CoD do?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the \u201ccountdown from Godhood to Beatable by Brendon Fraser\u201d that each Mummy waking is built around in Mummy the Curse is specifically attempting to capture the feel of gothic horror and pulp stories where mummies are the monsters. As Classic World of Darkness Mummies (whether the ancient Shensu-Heru, or the modern Amenti) are the most unambiguous good guys of all supernaturals in the WoD, they do not strongly feature said attempts to capture horror elements in their nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T09:53:38-07:00","id":1447592,"title":"","content":"Hello I don't want to hijack this thread but since there is no dedicated forum for WOD Mummys so I thought I chime in. I am looking for some Information on the Undying of MTR or Mummy in general for my Vampire Chronicle.<br /> <br /> I am the ST for a chronicle set in Egypt Alexandria during the Ptolemaic Era. Specifically during Ptolemy XIII Reign. We use the Rules from DAV20 .<br /> <br /> On of my PCs who is a Cappadocian descendet from Lazarus's Childer, and maybe too curious for his own good, got some vague hints on the &quot;Spell of Life&quot; from an &quot;allied&quot; Follower of Set. Naturally being a Cappadocian he wants to pursue those hints.<br /> <br /> I absolutely realise I am bending the canon here, because as far as I know Lazarus Child Angelique was embraced about a 150 years later. It was a concession I was willing to make for my players and for my chronicle because the setting has a place for characters of varous descents. Egyptian, Greek, Roman and so on.<br /> <br /> So this might bring him and the coterie into conflict with not only the Mages of the Cult of Isis but also the Shemsu-Heru.<br /> <br /> Since I gave him that hint I want to do those factions justice. I only recently got into MTR and find it to be very interesting, though I have a few problems.<br /> <br /> Exactly how powerful are they compared to other Supernaturals such as Vampires and Garou? Since they are the mortal enemy of the Setites I imagine them a force to be reckoned with. Are they too much to handle for my coterie of Neonates?<br /> <br /> None of my PCs is a Setite btw. so instant animosity might not be the case?<br /> <br /> I know Crossover Games can be difficult even if it is just NPCs.<br /> <br /> Is there a baseline to how the Undying approach potential enemys? Given their small numbers (as far as i know) they might not favor the combative approach? Or do they use their state of being nigh &quot;unkillable&quot; for a more direct approach? Are they solitary creatures or do they have something akin to coteries or packs?<br /> <br /> I wanted to look into MTR because it was the most recent write-up for the Undying in the WOD. Do you think the earlier Editions might be a better fit for a crossover?<br /> <br /> If I got some things wrong please do correct me!<br /> <br /> If the crossover presents itself as not doable I might swap the Undying out with the Children of Osiris Bloodline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25379,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25379-spacedigger","user":"Spacedigger","date":". 05-05-2021, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25379-spacedigger","name":"Spacedigger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T08:34:25-07:00","id":1447716,"title":"","content":"You do realize that you can start your own thread, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T08:46:16-07:00","id":1447717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1434223-are-mummies-still-canon?p=1446384#post1446384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They mean are you asking about the immortal ancient Egyptians from Mummy 1st edition and Mummy 2nd edition; or are you asking about the Amenti from Mummy the Resurrection who are modern day people who have had a piece of an ancient Egyptian soul shoved into them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mummy: the Resurrection included a Flaw you could take if you wanted to play the pre-Reckoning style of mummies. It didn't do a very good job of it; but it set the precedent that both versions can coexist. <br /> <br /> If they ever do a second edition of Mummy: the Resurrection, I'd like to see an appendix focusing on the old-school mummies, perhaps hinting that the transition from \u201cUndying\u201d to \u201cReborn\u201d (I think that's the correct terminology) wasn't nearly as universal \u2014 or as positive \u2014 as the Amanti like to make it out to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}